<div style="background-color: #f0f8ff; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center; border: 2px solid #1a5276;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; font-size: 1.2em; margin-top: 5px;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 75%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Traditional Style of Dress</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Let's Dress for a Dance.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: reading1: Demonstrate comprehension of simple written exchanges in letters, emails, or social media. reading2: Write short responses to questions about a text. phonemicAwareness: Blend spoken simple onsets and rhymes to form real words (onset /c/ and rhyme /at/).</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can demonstrate comprehension, in short exchanges, by identifying words for traditional clothing (e.g., 'pollera,' 'dress.'). Can answer questions, in a text, about traditional clothing (e.g., 'What is a pollera?' 'Panama's traditional dress.'). Can blend spoken simple onsets and rhymes to read and spell one-syllable, two-syllable, and simple multisyllabic words related to cultural clothing (e.g., /dr/ /ɛs/ in 'dress' for one syllable, /ɪ/ /vɛnt/ in 'event' for two syllables, and /trə/ /dɪʃ/ /ən/ /əl/ in 'traditional' for multisyllabic words).</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f0f8ff;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; color: #1a5276; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; color: #1a5276; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification of prior knowledge related to traditional clothing and the theme "Let's Dress for a Dance."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays flashcards or pictures of traditional Panamanian clothing (e.g., pollera, montuno) and some modern clothes. Students identify them. Teacher asks, "What are they wearing?" and "Is this traditional clothing or modern clothing?" (Using `Present Continuous` for description, `WH-questions` for elicitation, and vocabulary: `traditional clothing`, `modern`).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher holds up a picture of a pollera, points to it, and says, "This is a pollera. It is a beautiful traditional dress. Women wear this dress at important festivals and celebrations in our community." (Uses `Present Simple` and `Present Continuous` for describing, and vocabulary: `beautiful`, `traditional`, `dress`, `wear`, `important`, `festivals`, `celebrations`, `community`). The teacher models the /w/ sound in 'wearing' and the /t/ sound in 'traditional'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is a pollera a T-shirt?" (No, it's a dress.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do men wear polleras?" (No, women wear polleras.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is a pollera new or old-fashioned?" (It is traditional, old-fashioned, but still used for celebrations.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Our Traditional Style of Dress." Students engage with an authentic text to build comprehension.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short descriptive text (e.g., an excerpt from a children's cultural blog or an informal email) about attending a traditional Panamanian dance or `event` and describing the `attire` worn. The text will feature `Present Continuous` and `Present Simple` structures, and target vocabulary: `pollera`, `dress`, `attire`, `jewelry`, `festive`, `beautiful`, `cultural`, `wear`, `represent`, `admire`.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Example Text (displayed on board/handout):</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 10px; border-radius: 5px;">
                    Hi Ana,<br><br>
                    Guess what? I am going to a `cultural` `event` on Saturday! It's a dance `celebration` in our `community`. My cousin, Sofia, is `wearing` a beautiful `pollera`. It is our `traditional clothing` and she looks so `pretty`. The `jewelry` she is `wearing` is also very special. Polleras `showcase` Panama's rich `tradition`. People always `admire` them `during` the `festive` dance. What `attire` are you `wearing` for the party?
                    <br><br>Love,<br>Elena
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Demonstrate comprehension of simple written exchanges in informal texts, identifying key information about traditional clothing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Reading):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Questions:</b>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is Elena writing about?" (A cultural event/dance celebration).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Who is wearing a pollera?" (Sofia, Elena's cousin).</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read statements and circle True or False based on the text.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Elena is going to a modern party." (False)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Sofia is wearing traditional clothing." (True)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The pollera is ugly." (False)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Reading skills, reinforcing target grammar and vocabulary from the text.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice reading sentences containing `Present continuous`, `WH-questions` (implied in answers), `Present simple`, and vocabulary (`attire`, `celebration`, `event`, `community`, `traditional clothing`, `jewelry`, `showcase`, `represent`, `explain`, `admire`, `dress`, `use`, `wear`, `festive`, `pretty`, `beautiful`, `cultural`, `important`, `traditional`, `old-fashioned`, `modern`, `during`, `at`, `in`). Phonemic awareness: blend spoken onsets and rhymes for words related to clothing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Reading Practice (Gap-fill):</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with sentences from the Presentation text, but with key vocabulary words missing. Students read the sentences and choose the correct word from a box to fill in the blanks.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "Sofia is ______ a beautiful pollera." (wearing / drawing)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "Polleras are our ______ clothing." (modern / traditional)</li>
                        </ul>
                        This activity reinforces vocabulary and `Present continuous`/`Present simple` in context.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Reading and Matching (Vocabulary & Comprehension):</b> Students receive a handout with short descriptions of different traditional clothes from Panama (e.g., pollera, montuno, cutarras). Next to each description, there are pictures. Students read each description and draw a line to match it with the correct picture. (Vocabulary: `attire`, `dress`, `jewelry`, `festive`, `cultural`).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Phonemic Awareness (Reading Blends):</b> The teacher writes simple words on the board or provides a handout. Students read the words and identify the onset and rhyme.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher models: "Listen and read: /k/ + /at/ makes 'cat'." Students repeat.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher writes target vocabulary words on the board. Students work individually or in pairs to read these words and identify the blends.
                                <ul>
                                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">`dress`: Teacher points to `dr` and `ess`. Students read `/dr/` + `/ɛs/` = 'dress'.</li>
                                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">`event`: Teacher points to `e` and `vent`. Students read `/ɪ/` + `/vɛnt/` = 'event'.</li>
                                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">`pretty`: Teacher points to `pr` and `etty`. Students read `/pr/` + `/ɪtɪ/` = 'pretty'.</li>
                                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher also includes general words focusing on /c/ and /at/ if applicable, e.g., 'hat' if it can be related to clothing, or just for practice blending: 'cat', 'mat'.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students then practice reading and spelling these words silently or to a partner.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic reading scenario, connected to "Let's Dress for a Dance." and "Our Traditional Style of Dress."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> "Traditional Clothing Riddle Reading and Response." Students work in pairs. Each pair receives a set of cards. Some cards have short descriptions (riddles) of traditional Panamanian clothing, and other cards have the names or pictures of the clothing items.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students take turns picking a riddle card.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A reads the riddle aloud to Student B.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example Riddle: "I am a `beautiful` and `festive` `dress`. Women `wear` me `during` `celebrations`. I have many colors and `jewelry`. What am I?" (A pollera)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example Riddle: "I am men's `traditional clothing`. I am usually white and `embroidered`. People `wear` me for `cultural events`. What am I?" (A montuno)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student B listens and then reads the corresponding name or picture card to match the description.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They check if their match is correct (teacher provides answer key or checks by circulating).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">This activity uses vocabulary (`beautiful`, `festive`, `dress`, `wear`, `during`, `celebrations`, `jewelry`, `traditional clothing`, `cultural events`) and focuses on reading comprehension and identifying key details from a text.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in reading simple descriptive texts, collaborative interaction, and communicative task completion by accurately identifying clothing items from descriptions.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy to check students' reading comprehension and ability to respond in writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist and individual written response.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students will receive a new, short paragraph (similar to the Presentation text but about a different traditional attire or aspect). They read the paragraph and then answer 2-3 simple WH-questions in writing below the text.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 10px; border-radius: 5px;">
                    <b>Read about the Montuno:</b><br><br>
                    The `montuno` is `traditional clothing` for men in Panama. Men `wear` it `at` `cultural events` and dances. It is a white shirt with special `embroidered` designs. Sometimes men `wear` a `chata` hat and `cutarras` (sandals) with their montuno. It is an `important` part of our `community`'s `attire`.
                    <br><br>
                    <b>Answer the questions:</b><br>
                    1. What is the montuno?<br>
                    2. Who wears the montuno?<br>
                    3. When do men wear the montuno?<br>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Reading Comprehension:</b> Correctly identifies key information (e.g., clothing name, who wears it, when).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Vocabulary:</b> Demonstrates understanding of vocabulary words by using them in responses or selecting correct options.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity of Response:</b> Provides short, intelligible answers to the questions.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete the following sentences on a small paper slip:
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, I can read about _______ (e.g., polleras) and understand what it is."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can answer questions about _______ (e.g., traditional clothing) after reading."</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student and teacher reflection on the lesson, identifying areas of success and future adjustments.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b> Students reflect on their learning by considering these questions:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy for me today when reading about traditional clothing?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was difficult or challenging when reading and answering questions?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this reading lesson? (e.g., Most students comprehended the texts and answered the questions accurately. The phonemic awareness activity helped them blend sounds.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? (e.g., Some students struggled with longer sentences; provide sentence frames for written responses or shorter texts. Integrate more visual aids for understanding new vocabulary in context.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did the activities effectively target the Reading skill and learning outcomes for A1.2?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence (Lesson 3: Speaking & Interaction):</b> "Today, we read about traditional clothing like the pollera and montuno. Next lesson, we will talk more about these clothes and describe what people are wearing at a dance!"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>